course: dictionary
lesson: 14535
title: Persistence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Persistence means not giving up. When something is hard, a person with persistence keeps trying anyway. «Mia kept practising her spellings every night, even when the list felt impossible.» Her persistence means she did not stop when it got difficult.
explain: Persistence can also mean something that goes on for a long time. «The persistence of the rain meant the football match was cancelled for a whole week.» Here nobody is trying at all: the rain just keeps going and going.
explain: Look for clue words around persistence, such as «even when», «again and again», «kept going» or «for a long time». Then ask: is someone trying hard, or is something lasting a long time? That question tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Persistence is a noun. It comes from the verb persist, which means to keep going.
fact: «Persistence» means going on trying even when something is hard or other people want you to stop.
fact: «Persistence» can also mean something continuing for a long time, like «the persistence of a bad smell».
fact: Thomas Edison tested many different materials before he found one that worked well in a light bulb. His persistence paid off.
fact: In school, persistence is praised: keep going when maths is difficult, and do not give up after one mistake.
exercise: «Sam practised his times tables every day for a month, even when he got them wrong.» What does this show? | *Persistence | Sleepiness | Boredom | Silence
exercise: «The persistence of the smoke made the whole room smell.» What does persistence mean here? | Trying very hard to do something | *Something continuing for a long time | A loud noise | A thick grey cloud
exercise: «Thomas Edison tested many materials, and his persistence paid off.» Find and copy one word that means keeping going even when it is hard. | Edison | *persistence | materials | tested
test: Nina practises the guitar every evening, even after her fingers get sore. What quality does she show? | Carelessness | Sleepiness | *Persistence | Fear
test: What does persistence mean? | Stopping as soon as things get difficult | *Going on trying even when it is hard | Being very quiet | Running very fast
exam: «Ben failed his test twice, but he studied again and again until he passed.» Which word best describes Ben? | Panic | *Persistence | Confusion | Laziness
